# Funda360 — environment configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (already gitignored — never commit real
# values) and fill in the placeholders below. Vite only exposes variables
# prefixed `VITE_` to the browser bundle — see src/vite-env.d.ts for the
# full typed list this app reads.
#
# Local development (recommended): run a local Supabase stack with the
# Supabase CLI (`supabase start`), which prints a local API URL and anon
# key to use here, and applies supabase/migrations/*.sql + supabase/seed.sql
# automatically via `supabase db reset`. See supabase/seed.sql for the
# seeded local login accounts — never point this app at a hosted project
# using that seed data.
#
# Never put a `service_role` key in this file or anywhere under VITE_ — it
# would ship to every browser that loads the app and bypass RLS entirely.
# Only the anon key belongs here; RLS (supabase/migrations/) is what
# actually restricts access.

# Required — Supabase project API URL (local: printed by `supabase start`;
# hosted: Project Settings → API → Project URL).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Required — Supabase anon/public API key (local: printed by
# `supabase start`; hosted: Project Settings → API → anon public key). Safe
# to expose to the browser — RLS is the actual access boundary, not this key.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional — display name shown in the UI shell. Falls back to a built-in
# default if unset.
VITE_APP_NAME=Funda360

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Online payment gateway (Edge Function secrets — NOT VITE_, never in the
# browser bundle, never in git). Set with `supabase secrets set NAME=value`
# for the deployment, or export locally before `supabase functions serve`.
# Only the provider a school actually uses needs its block. Full details:
# docs/PAYMENT_GATEWAY.md.
#
#   PayFast:   PAYFAST_PASSPHRASE
#   Ozow:      OZOW_PRIVATE_KEY, OZOW_API_KEY
#   Yoco:      YOCO_SECRET_KEY, YOCO_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   Peach:     PEACH_ACCESS_TOKEN, PEACH_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   Netcash:   NETCASH_PAYNOW_SERVICE_KEY
#
# The non-secret identifiers (PayFast merchant_id, Ozow site_code, …) are
# entered per-school in the app under Payment Settings, not here.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admissions public intake (Edge Function `admissions-public`). Deploy with
#   supabase functions deploy admissions-public --no-verify-jwt
# It needs NO extra secrets — only the SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# the platform injects automatically (same as the payments functions). Each
# school shares its own /apply?school=<school id> link. See docs/ADMISSIONS.md.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notification delivery worker (Edge Function `notifications-dispatch`).
# Drains the notification_deliveries outbox to email / SMS / WhatsApp. It
# stays INERT until deployed AND these secrets are set — until then every
# notification is in-app only and `pending` rows just accumulate. Set with
# `supabase secrets set NAME=value`. Full details: docs/NOTIFICATIONS_DELIVERY.md.
#
#   Always:    NOTIFICATIONS_DISPATCH_SECRET   (shared secret in the x-dispatch-secret header)
#   Email:     RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_FROM
#   SMS:       TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_SMS_FROM
#   WhatsApp:  TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM
#
# Per-school channel enable/disable + non-secret config lives in the app
# under Settings → Messaging & delivery (school_messaging_settings).

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build & test — no additional environment variables are required beyond
# the two above.
#
#   npm install        install dependencies
#   npm run dev         start the Vite dev server (needs the vars above)
#   npm run build        typecheck + production build
#   npm run typecheck    tsc -b --noEmit
#   npm run lint          eslint .
#   npm run test           vitest run (no Supabase connection needed — pure
#                           unit tests only)
#   npm run test:e2e        playwright — fully network-mocked (e2e/utils/),
#                           never touches a real Supabase project. Needs the
#                           dev server to boot, which only requires the two
#                           vars above to be present with ANY non-empty
#                           value (src/lib/supabase.ts just checks they're
#                           set) — real credentials are not required
#   supabase/rls-tests/run.sh   RLS/trigger/SECURITY DEFINER regression
#                                suite — needs Docker, spins up its own
#                                disposable Postgres container, reads no
#                                environment variables from this file
